{#- MiniMax H3 reference to video (full-reference mode): the six sections in order (MiniMax-H3
    docs/VIDEO_PROMPT_WRITING_GUIDE_ref_en.md, 2026-10-26). <Picture 1> is the first frame, the
    locked pictures follow; <Audio N> are the speakers' voice-timbre references, or (``dub``,
    先配音 through the H3 API) <Audio 1> is the dubbed lines, copied as the whole sound track.
    A locked picture only shows how a character or place looks, so it is cited inside a
    <Subject N> line, never a standalone <Picture N> line (the guide keeps those for frames; as
    its own line the model took it for a keyframe and cut to it, M5 step 14b). This layout is
    what the rewriter (``vprompt``, local H3) or H3's Context-IR (the API) starts from. -#}
subject_definitions:
<Picture 1> is the first frame of [Shot 1].
{% for r in refs %}
<Subject {{ loop.index }}> is {{ r.name }}, whose look comes from <Picture {{ loop.index + 1 }}>.
{% endfor %}
{% for v in voices %}
<Audio {{ loop.index }}> is the voice-timbre reference for {{ v.who }} (S{{ v.sx }}).
{% endfor %}
{% if dub %}
<Audio 1> is the dialogue track of the target video.
{% endif %}

summary: [keyframe completion{% if refs %} + reference generation{% endif %}{% if voices %} + audio reference{% endif %}{% if dub %} + audio reuse{% endif %}] The target video starts exactly on <Picture 1> and continues as one shot.

retention_analysis:
<Picture 1> ([Shot 1] first frame): fully_preserved - the opening composition, the people and the scene.
{% for r in refs %}
<Subject {{ loop.index }}> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - how {{ r.name }} looks.
{% endfor %}
{% for v in voices %}
<Audio {{ loop.index }}>: reference - {{ v.who }}'s voice timbre, without copying the original signal.
{% endfor %}
{% if dub %}
<Audio 1>: fully_copy - <Audio 1> is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track.
{% endif %}

detailed_description: [Shot 1] {{ description }}
{%- for d in dialogue %} {{ d.who }} (S{{ d.sx }}) {% if d.vo %}says in an off-screen voiceover{% else %}says{% endif %}{% if d.audio %}, using the voice timbre referenced from <Audio {{ d.audio }}>{% endif %}: <d>[{{ language }}] {{ d.text }}</d>{% if d.vo %} while the lips remain completely closed.{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}


overall_soundscape: {% if dub %}<Audio 1> as it is, with no other sound.{% else %}{{ soundscape }}{% endif %}

non_diegetic_music: N/A
